b: Band Select (full stop or comma, h help; q or another command exits)
e: frequency in MHz (e.g. 7.2)
m: Mode Select (full stop or comma, h help; q or another command exits)
full stop or comma: increase/decrease frequency by the configured step
z: round the current frequency to the nearest 1 kHz
s: Settings; v selects FTX-1 Main/Sub or Icom VFO A/B (first press selects A)
s then s: save the step size in hertz for the current mode
w: read signal strength, frequency and mode
q: quit YAC
o: Offset; o cycles Receive/Transmit/Clear; full stop adds 10 Hz, comma subtracts 10 Hz; either clears in Clear; q exits
i: Tone input; i cycles CTCSS/DCS N/DCS I; enter a value, Enter, then t for TX or b for Both when offered; q exits, h gives help
Profile selection: enter a number to highlight a radio, Space to select it, or q to cancel. Press h on the profile screen for this help.
p: cycle preamp stages and off
u: cycle attenuator levels and off
v: verify attenuator, preamp, configured power and supported tuner status
s then t: cycle supported tuner settings; repeat t, q leaves Settings
Tuner status describes the radio setting. Independent RF-sensing tuners are not detected. Off preserves the selected tuner except ATAS, which must be deselected to switch off. Tuner selection never starts tuning.
Power is reported in watts for Yaesu/Kenwood and as the relative setting percentage for Icom; it is not measured transmitted power. Unknown means a supported setting could not be read.
Opening Offset starts in Receive at zero hertz. Another command key exits.
Mode selection starts at the radio's current mode and loops through the modes.
Band selection starts at the current band. Icom and Kenwood band selection
stops at each end; Yaesu follows the radio's band behavior.
At an upper band limit, use comma to go down, or e to enter a frequency.

a adjusts AF Gain. r adjusts Squelch in FM, RF Gain in other modes. Starts at the current radio value, shown as a rounded percentage. Full stop increases; comma decreases. Steps are about 3 percent. Stops at each end without looping. q leaves and keeps the setting. Another command key leaves and starts that command.

Settings: s then p opens the power edit field. Enter a whole number in the displayed units and range, then Enter; blank cancels. Successful changes are silent. Leave Settings with q and press v to check power.

Power edit: whole watts; h then Enter for help; blank Enter cancels. Icom watt entries are estimated and converted to a relative percentage; v reports that percentage. Success is silent. Leave Settings with q before v.
